    id: "security-web", category: "Identity & Security", title: "Untrusted input, output, and web sessions",
    summary: "Separate validation, parameterization, output encoding, and request-origin protections.",
    what: "Validation checks whether input meets a contract. SQL parameterization separates data from query syntax. Context-appropriate output handling prevents text from becoming executable markup. Session protections address theft and cross-origin misuse. These are complementary boundaries, not one universal sanitize operation.",
