    summary: "Turn retry, timeout, replay, and race assumptions into controlled experiments.",
    what: "A failure-oriented test selects a specific interruption or ordering and checks the promised invariant. Concurrent correctness cannot be established by repeatedly running a happy-path operation and hoping a race appears. The test should control the relevant boundary and interleaving.",
    why: "Crashes near commits and acknowledgments produce duplicate effects or lost work. A late UI response can reveal content after navigation. A timeout is particularly misleading because it describes the caller's wait, not necessarily the remote operation's outcome.",
