    summary: "Distinguish traversal state, graph cycles, shortest paths, and reusable subproblem states.",
    what: "Trees have constrained structure; general graphs may include cycles, disconnected regions, and multiple paths. DFS explores deeply and BFS explores by distance layers in an unweighted graph. Dynamic programming stores results for a well-defined set of overlapping subproblems and combines them through valid transitions.",
